Z||000001||watts||11-14-2001||01:01 PM||||Someone correct me if I'm wrong...<P>But I've never seen a thermac system used on either the 4 or the 6 cyl's in a Fiero.<P>I know exactly what you mean about them...  just never seen it used!<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||11-14-2001||01:11 PM||||It was used on the 84-86 2.5's if I'm not mistaken. The stove end clamps onto the exhaust that runs horizontal across the engine bay (the top one). That is then connected to your flex tube to the bottom of the air cleaner.<BR>Hope this helps you out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||11-14-2001||01:15 PM||||I have a thermac system on my '84, don't have any pictures of it on hand.<P>The hot stove pipe tube goes from under the aircleaner straight down to the short horizontal tube right after the exhaust bends from the exhaust manifold.||||reg||1
